dencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# 🐞 bug report\r\n\r\n### Affected Package\r\n<!-- Can you pin-point one or more @angular/* packages as the source of the bug? -->\r\n<!-- ✍️edit: --> The issue is caused by package @angular/router\r\n\r\n\r\n### Is this a regression?\r\n\r\n<!-- Did this behavior use to work in the previous version? -->\r\n<!-- ✍️-->  No.\r\n\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\n<!-- ✍️-->\r\nI use a guard to protect a route. If the user is not allowed to access the route I'd like to redirect to the root url. I'm doing this by returning an UrlTree from the canActivate method. To get the UrlTree for the root url I'm calling router.parseUrl('/'). However when I navigate to the protected page the redirect to the root url does not happen. The protected page isn't displayed either and there are no errors in the console.\r\n\r\nIf I change the guard to return router.parseUrl('/unauthorized') the redirect to the unauthorized page works as expected. I think this should also work for the root url. Am I missing something or is this a bug?\r\n\r\n\r\n## 🔬 Minimal Reproduction\r\n<!--\r\nPlease create and share minimal reproduction of the issue starting with this template: https://stackblitz.com/fork/angular-issue-repro2\r\n-->\r\n<!-- ✍️-->\r\n[https://stackblitz.com/edit/angular-issue-repro2-w72ytp](https://stackblitz.com/edit/angular-issue-repro2-w72ytp)\r\n<!--\r\nIf StackBlitz is not suitable for reproduction of your issue, please create a minimal GitHub repository with the reproduction of the issue. Share the link to the repo below along with step-by-step instructions to reproduce the problem, as well as expected and actual behavior.\r\n\r\nIssues that don't have enough info and can't be reproduced will be closed.\r\n\r\nYou can read more about issue submission guidelines here: https://github.com/angular/angular/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#-submitting-an-issue\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## 🔥 Exception or Error\r\n